e for library workers, James can't have a part-time job. So, James doesn't have a part-time job, but he does take the database course. Therefore, the statement is true because he satisfies the first part of the \"either/or.\"\n\nI think that's solid. So the answer should be A) True.\n</think>\n\nThe statement is true because James takes the database course, satisfying one part of the \"either/or\" condition.\n\n**Answer: A) True**",
