towards animals except through the mean behavior. So, Tom's niceness towards animals doesn't affect his grumpiness.\n\nTherefore, based on the given information, we can't definitively say whether Tom is grumpy or not. The premises don't provide enough information to conclude his personality beyond his behavior towards animals. So, the statement \"Tom is a grumpy person\" is uncertain.\n</think>\n\nThe statement \"Tom is a grumpy person\" is uncertain because the given information doesn't provide enough details about Tom's personality beyond his behavior towards animals. \n\n# Answer:\nC) Uncertain",
